{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1543191-pdf-editing","id":1543191,"title":"PDF Editing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-06T02:25:37-07:00","id":1543191,"title":"PDF Editing","content":"Hello everyone, <br /> <br /> I have a few questions regarding the PDF files that can be purchased through drivethrurpg, for example.<br /> <br /> I noticed that older versions of various PDF files contain errors in the text, such as grammatical errors, unclear wording, or outright misleading rule descriptions.<br /> <br /> However, new versions of the PDFs seem to have been improved and upgraded, which is excellent! For instance, the MtA 2e Core Rulebook now has an enhanced table of contents structure, including some highlighting and clarifications of texts under Mage Armor, for example, with the following addition: &quot;Mage Armors that increase Defense work against surprise attacks.&quot; On top of that, corrected grammar, for example, in the text under the merit &quot;Artifact.&quot; And more. <br /> <br /> Long story short: Significant improvements have been made even after the original publication. In fact, my earlier version of MtA 2e Core has 25 fewer pages than the new, updated version.<br /> <br /> Now, my questions are the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Is there any way to distinguish the versions? I haven't noticed anything like a version number or any other indication in the books (other than the changes in the texts themselves).<br /> 2. Is Onyx still editing and improving the PDF files if needed? This is especially relevant for the latest releases (The Hege, etc.), but also for the old ones.<br /> 3. Is there an official summary of all changes? Maybe a document? Can we know what reasoning was behind the changes? I assume there were discussions in the forums to which Onyx referred.<br /> 4. After purchasing 